// Measured WorkGroupMapping (WGM) landscapes on gfx1151 (Strix Halo, 40 CUs, one XCD).
// Method: hipblaslt-bench with flush and 512 MB rotating buffers, the WGM forced per run; shader clock pinned at
// 1900 MHz; median of 3 interleaved processes per WGM value.
// Builds: rows flagged MAGIC were measured on hipBLASLt develop d8ad7ea114f plus the magic-number WGM remap for
// gfx115X (2026-11-25); all other rows on develop 602c8b16a2a (2026-11-18 and 2026-11-19), whose kernels compute
// the remap in fp64.  The fp64 prologue costs a few ns per workgroup more, so non-MAGIC rows overstate the cost
// of WGM > 1 relative to WGM 1 for current gfx115X kernels.
// Cases: 250 shapes with natural and with padded lda/ldb, the hard ones repeated; the same kernels with
// re-strided and with padded outputs (ldc = ldd); 78 store-dominated and large-A cases; 175 of them re-measured
// with the magic-number remap.  MacroTile and DepthU are those of the kernel that ran, the occupancy is the one
// it reported.
// Classes: W values that launch the same tile order share one entry.  W <= 1 is key 1, W >= nwg1 is key nwg1,
// W <= -nwg0 is key -nwg0; on an identity grid (nwg0 == 1 or nwg1 == 1) every W > 1 is key 2 and every
// W < 0 is key -2 (same order, but the remap prologue runs).
// Tolerance: a class is accepted if time <= best * (1 + tol), tol = min(max(1 %, spread of the best class,
// spread of the class), 3 %), spread = (max - min) / min over processes and repeats.  The 3 % cap keeps a
// single slow process from accepting a reproducibly slower W.
//
// Columns: WGM_CASE(id, m, n, k, batch, transA, transB, element types of A, B, C, D, lda, ldb, ldc, ldd in
// elements, MacroTile0, MacroTile1, DepthU, GlobalSplitU, 1 for a WMMA kernel, runtime occupancy in workgroups
// per WGP (0 = unknown), WGM pinned in the shipped kernel, flags, best W, best time in microseconds,
// "W:regret[*] ...").  regret is in tenths of a percent over the best class; '*' marks an accepted class.
// Flags: PAD lda/ldb padded to an odd multiple of 128 bytes; PROD production-like (PAD, or natural lda/ldb
// whose A and B row bytes are not multiples of 1024); IDENT identity grid; AUX kernel with the extra output E
// and GELU; OUT1K / OUT4K output row bytes a multiple of 1024 / 4096; OUTRS ldc = ldd != m; SHORT best time
// below 100 us (out of scope, not asserted); NT transA = N and transB = T (automatic WGM stays off, the pinned
// WGM applies, not asserted); STORE store-dominated, output tile bytes (x 2 with E) >= 0.15 x (A tile + B tile
// bytes); ARTIFACT K < 16 with padded lda/ldb (the padding inflates A and B up to 64x, not asserted); MAGIC
// landscape measured with the magic-number remap.
